   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Chat**: rare: 14 archived performances [3]\n- **Chat**: rare: 14 archived performances [3]\n- **Chat & Tuning**: back after 20 archived shows (1806 days); rare: 12 archived performances [3]\n- **I Hear You Calling**: rare: 8 archived performances [3]\n- **Chat & Tuning**: back after 20 archived shows (1806 days); rare: 12 archived performances [3]\n- **Mind Games**: rare: 8 archived performances [3]\n- **Chat & Tuning**: back after 20 archived shows (1806 days); rare: 12 archived performances [3]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **twod2014-03-29.CA_11.16bit** (recommended): source not stated; 21 songs; 110 min [1]\n- **twod2014-03-29.CA-11.24bit**: source not stated; 21 songs; 110 min [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Positioned directly in front of left speakers; Adam Granduciel played harp [1]\n- Recorded in front of left speakers; Adam Granduciel performed on harp [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **twod2014-03-29.CA_11.16bit**: taped by Bryan Caetano; transferred by Dennis Orr; source: CA-11 Cardioids (in hat) > CA-9000 (with high pass turned on) > Zoom H1 @ 24 bit/48 kHz [1]. Also: Recorded with CA-11 cardioids into Zoom H1, mastered to 16-bit FLAC [1]\n- **twod2014-03-29.CA-11.24bit**: taped by Bryan Caetano; transferred by Dennis Orr; source: CA-11 Cardioids (in hat) > CA-9000 (with high pass turned on) > Zoom H1 @ 24 bit/48 kHz [2]. Also: Captured via CA-11 cardioids and Zoom H1, mastered to 24-bit FLAC [2]",
